  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking bug**:\n\n**[P1] `topTags` mutates the caller’s array — `src/tags.js:10`.**  \n`.sort()` operates in place, violating the documented non-mutation contract. In `sidebar()`, the cloud is computed before the recent strip (`src/render.js:4–5`), so “recent” becomes ordered by popularity instead of its original order.\n\nVerified: input `a:1, b:9, c:4` produces `recent: ['b', 'c', 'a']` instead of `['a', 'b', 'c']`.\n\n**Recommended fix:** sort a copy (`[...tags].sort(...)`). Add regression assertions that `topTags` preserves its input and `sidebar` preserves recent order.\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but they don’t catch this regression. No files changed.",
